at 4 we see the  introduction of quan chi as a playable  character and he deceived scorpion into  believing that sub-zero was responsible  for the eradication of his clan and the  death of his wife and son and this game  had character-specific endings which was  really really awesome and it depended on  who you played as  wrong jerick this is not a brutality  this is a fatality  and this became a little confusing  because they didn't all line up with one  another because at this point the  developers didn't really seem  interested in creating one cohesive  story for the franchise  but if you beat the game of scorpion  you're seen standing over sub-zero  bragging about avenging the death of his  family now sub-zero tells him his  family's killer is still free at which  point quan chi appears and reveals  himself to be the one responsible for  the death of scorpion's family and that  he simply needed the strength of a  spectre to defeat his nemesis sub-zero  so he'd manipulate a scorpion into doing  it for him now quan chi sends scorpion  back to the nether realm the scorpion  grabs quan chi and they're both taken  through the portal sub-zero's ending  basically tells a slightly different  story the scorpion had agreed to fight  on kwon chi's behalf  in exchange for his freedom from the  nether realm but that quan qi  had no intention of honoring the deal  and didn't need to know that sub-zero  had killed him and that both scorpion  and sub-zero had been used as pawns for  shinnok a fallen elder god now as it  turns out  scorpion wasn't as dead as he appeared  and he kills quan chi  telling sub-zero their beef was  basically settled and the sub-zero was  free of scorpion's curse so that's  awesome now in 2002's mortal kombat  deadly alliance we see how scorpion's  ending from mortal kombat 4 was actually  supposed to play out as he's now  committed to finding and killing quan  chief  instead finds himself being met with two  demons named draman  or drama as i like to 