iver  the killing blow now eventually both  scorpion and sub-zero are liberated from  quan chi's influence and they put their  differences aside to form an alliance  now after the next several years  scorpion rebuilds this clan but this  time around they're dedicated to the  defense  of earth realm and so when mortal kombat  11 a new villain emerges in the form of  chronica the mother of the elder god of  death and corruption shinnok now  chronica's intent is to merge the past  and present timelines  and as part of that she basically brings  a younger version of scorpion into the  present day but while trying to recruit  allies to the army being built by raiden  to oppose chronica a present-day  scorpion  is killed by devorah who serves chronica  and so with his last breath the older  scorpion  implies his younger self to abandon his  quest for vengeance and fight alongside  the defenders of earth realm  against cronica and his younger self  ultimately agrees so the game ends when  chronic is defeated but once again  there are character specific endings  although not considered completely  incontinuity i'll mention that in  scorpion's ending he kills cronica and  is in possession of an hourglass capable  of rebooting the timeline  he does this in hopes of bringing his  family back but every time he does they  end up getting destroyed and so he  figures out that an ultra powerful race  known as the titans are responsible for  the inescapable death of his family and  resolves to exact revenge upon them so  that's basically scorpion's story as it  plays out in a video game franchise and  so now  we can move on to his abilities as a  combatant of course like  every combatant in mortal kombat he's  skilled in both armed and unarmed combat  with his signature weapon being a spear  attached to a chain  that he launches at his opponents and  then uses it to bring them within  punching distance while shouting get  over here  which i gotta be honest man like when  they did that in like the mortal kombat  movie like i was expecting like this  epic moment right where like scorpion's  just like get over here and it's like  this super dramatic thing and he's like  get over here buddy and i was like dude  this sucks man like it was the least  exciting get over here that i've ever  heard like i was like okay come on like  you know  but regardless my little tangent aside  in addition to his spirit scorpion  routinely employs other  weapons most notably his twin short  swords and the more recent appearances  scorpion's also able to manipulate  hellfire and he frequently does this by  summoning it beneath his opponent  curling fireballs at him  or taking off his mask and then spitting  in his opponents from a skeleton-like  head now finally  scorpion's also a skilled necromancer  and is capable of summoning demons and  other spectral creatures to attack his  opponents and if all of that sounds  really badass well that's the reason  scorpions become not only one of the  most popular mortal kombat characters in  the entire franchise but one of the most  popular characters in video game  history so with that being said guys  we're gonna bring this to an end thanks  for watching and i will catch you all  later  peace

